From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:27:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(goldens): retire claude-to-codex-caller-cwd; the resume
 directory is the codex cwd by design

The pin said claude -> codex writes "/" where the source session's cwd
was, and took the source cwd as what a fix would write. A real run
(path resume --harness codex -C <dir>, export codex --project <dir>)
writes <dir> into session_meta, every turn_context and the state_5
thread row, and that is what codex needs: codex resume's picker lists
only sessions whose cwd is the directory it runs in (--all disables
the filter). The goldens wrote "/" because the hermetic run starts
there. Not a defect: the pin, its Finding and the manifest entry go;
write_defects now prunes retired defects from the manifest; a
projection::codex unit test pins the -C dir as the written cwd; the
qualifier concerns are resolved reason:invalid with the explanation.
Behaviour unchanged; known_defects@claude.snap loses the one entry.
